{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'ls gate-run15*; cat render-r1.txt; cat round46s-brief.md; tail -8 mutants.log'","aggregated_output":"gate-run15.fixtures.json\ngate-run15.txt\nsystem 4373 characters; user 121246 characters; schema 9626 characters\nevidence items 237; themes 9\nsource passages the answer cites that the rendered request does not show: none\nschema errors: none\ncalc_check errors: none\nrecorded: [{\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}]\nsame-base family (calls 8729, 8732): Relations: v35 rests on v14's base.\n# Council round 46s: after 46r (read-only, same thread)\n\n46r answered: C6 checks band overlap on the outcome's value set with open and closed ends kept (_outcome_set, _overlaps): a '<40' outcome is refused on the $40–50B rung (R4b2) and accepted on the $30–40B rung (R4b3).\n\nGate run 15: 65 of 65. Mutants: 30 of 30 caught. render-r1 clean.\n\nAnswer GATE PASS STANDS or GATE FAIL, sorting any finding as (A) blocking or (B) a relabelling for the blind readers. Only (A) blocks. If no (A) remains, say GATE PASS STANDS.\nC1 accepts any substring (alone) | T9 | CAUGHT (['T9'])\nC5 allows estimates | P3b | CAUGHT (['P3b'])\nper-unit identity ignores scope | P4 | CAUGHT (['P4'])\nper-unit inverse loses its scale | G3inv | CAUGHT (['G3inv'])\nC2 tolerance 50% | P2 | CAUGHT (['P2', 'U2'])\nbound direction ignored | R4m | CAUGHT (['R4m'])\nC9 same base off (both clauses) | G4m | CAUGHT (['G24m', 'G24d', 'G24c', 'G24x', 'G4x', 'G4c', 'G4m'])\nC10 prior not authenticated | P3c | CAUGHT (['P3c'])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '46r|_outcome_set|_overlaps|R4b[23]|C6' calc_check.py gate.py mutants.py gate-run15.txt DESIGN.md; nl -ba calc_check.py | sed -n '100,151p;199,226p;359,401p' \"","aggregated_output":"DESIGN.md:76:| **C6 rung and outcome** [46.2] | the chosen rung's band overlaps the outcome (a point: contains it). The reasons say why that band, where the range overlaps several | a rung no part of the outcome falls in |\nDESIGN.md:162:| G1–G4 (controls) | q01, q02, q19, q22, from `gold-v1.json`'s reasoning (expressions from the packet items). q01's Q1 + Q2 as `time_aggregation`; q02's comparison $392B (consensus) × 92% (reported mix); q22 in one family with q01, reading q01's FY2027 node | all pass, estimates visible; q02's reference passes C5; q19's overlapping range passes C6 with its reason |\nmutants.py:37:    ('C6 ignores bounds', \"        if not _overlaps(_outcome_set(out), band):                 # [46r] open and closed ends kept\",\nmutants.py:38:     \"        if not _overlaps((_interval(out)[0], True, _interval(out)[1], True), band):\", 'R4b2'),\ngate-run15.txt:103:PASS  R1rneg  C6: no such rung\ngate-run15.txt:104:        C6: v9: rung -2 is not one of 1..5\ngate-run15.txt:106:PASS  R1r6   C6: no such rung\ngate-run15.txt:107:        C6: v9: rung 6 is not one of 1..5\ngate-run15.txt:109:PASS  R1rnone  C6: no such rung\ngate-run15.txt:110:        C6: v9: rung None is not one of 1..5\ngate-run15.txt:112:PASS  R4b2   C6: below 40 is not on the 40-50 rung\ngate-run15.txt:113:        C6: v41: rung 2 ([40, 50]) contains no part of its outcome (-inf, False, 40.0, False)\ngate-run15.txt:115:PASS  R4b3   below 40 sits on the 30-40 rung\ncalc_check.py:163:def _outcome_set(fig):\ncalc_check.py:179:def _overlaps(values, band):\ncalc_check.py:352:    # answers: C7 coverage and ownership, C6 rung, C5 reference\ncalc_check.py:381:            errors.append(('C6', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: rung {rung!r} is not one of 1..{len(member[\"bands\"])}'))\ncalc_check.py:384:        if not _overlaps(_outcome_set(out), band):                 # [46r] open and closed ends kept\ncalc_check.py:385:            errors.append(('C6', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: rung {rung} ({band}) contains no part of its outcome {_outcome_set(out)}'))\ngate.py:462:        item(name, R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, rr, lambda r: (any(c == 'C6' and 'is not one of' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C6: no such rung'), '')\ngate.py:463:    for name, rung_b, expect_c6 in (('R4b2', 2, True), ('R4b3', 3, False)):   # [46r] \"less than $40B\" on rung 2 and on rung 3\ngate.py:469:             (lambda r: (any(c == 'C6' for c, _ in r['errors']), 'C6: below 40 is not on the 40-50 rung')) if expect_c6 else\ngate.py:470:             (lambda r: (not any(c == 'C6' for c, _ in r['errors']), 'below 40 sits on the 30-40 rung')), '')\n   100\t    if not ok:\n   101\t        return [('C1', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: value {fig.get(\"value\")} {unit} bound {bound} does not equal \"{expr[\"text\"]}\" as component {comp}')]\n   102\t    return []\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\tdef _interval(fig):\n   106\t    if 'low' in fig and 'high' in fig:\n   107\t        return fig['low'], fig['high']\n   108\t    return fig['value'], fig['value']\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef _compute(op, inputs, signs, out_unit=None):\n   112\t    \"\"\"inputs: [(lo, hi, unit)]; returns (lo, hi) in out_unit.\"\"\"\n   113\t    los = [i[0] for i in inputs]\n   114\t    his = [i[1] for i in inputs]\n   115\t    if op in ('sum', 'roll_forward'):\n   116\t        s = signs or [1] * len(inputs)\n   117\t        return (sum((a if k > 0 else b) * k for a, b, k in zip(los, his, s)), sum((b if k > 0 else a) * k for a, b, k in zip(los, his, s)))\n   118\t    if op == 'difference':\n   119\t        return los[0] - his[1], his[0] - los[1]\n   120\t    if op == 'product':\n   121\t        lo = hi = 1.0\n   122\t        for a, b in zip(los, his):\n   123\t            lo, hi = lo * a, hi * b\n   124\t        units = [i[2] for i in inputs]\n   125\t        if 'units' in units and 'USD' in units and out_unit == 'USD bn':     # units times a dollar price, in billions\n   126\t            lo, hi = lo / 1e9, hi / 1e9\n   127\t        return lo, hi\n   128\t    if op == 'ratio':\n   129\t        units = [i[2] for i in inputs]\n   130\t        if 'USD' in units and 'USD bn' in units:                # a dollar total over a per-unit price\n   131\t            los = [x * 1e9 if u == 'USD bn' else x for x, u in zip(los, units)]\n   132\t            his = [x * 1e9 if u == 'USD bn' else x for x, u in zip(his, units)]\n   133\t        return los[0] / his[1], his[0] / los[1]\n   134\t    if op == 'share':\n   135\t        return los[0] * los[1] / 100.0, his[0] * his[1] / 100.0\n   136\t    if op == 'growth':\n   137\t        return (los[1] / his[0] - 1) * 100.0, (his[1] / los[0] - 1) * 100.0\n   138\t    if op == 'apply_growth':\n   139\t        return los[0] * (1 + los[1] / 100.0), his[0] * (1 + his[1] / 100.0)\n   140\t    if op == 'range_from_relative':\n   141\t        return los[0] * (1 - los[1] / 100.0), his[0] * (1 + his[1] / 100.0)\n   142\t    raise ValueError(op)\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\tDIRECTION = {'>': 'lower', '>=': 'lower', 'approx_above': 'lower', '<': 'upper', '<=': 'upper', 'approx_below': 'upper',\n   146\t             'approx': 'two-sided', None: None}\n   147\tFLIP = {'lower': 'upper', 'upper': 'lower', 'two-sided': 'two-sided', None: None}\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\tdef _bound_direction(op, ins):\n   151\t    \"\"\"For positive operands: which side the result is bounded on, from its inputs' bounds (None: a point).\"\"\"\n   199\t    parts = period.split()\n   200\t    if len(parts) == 1 and parts[0].startswith('FY'):\n   201\t        return parts[0], {1, 2, 3, 4}\n   202\t    if len(parts) == 2 and parts[0].startswith('FY') and parts[1] in QUARTERS:\n   203\t        return parts[0], QUARTERS[parts[1]]\n   204\t    return None\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\tdef _key(what):\n   208\t    return (what['population'], what['measure'], what['scope'], what['period'])\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\tdef check(family, passages, calc):\n   212\t    errors, recorded = [], []\n   213\t    figs = {}\n   214\t    for fig in calc['figures']:\n   215\t        if fig['id'] in figs:\n   216\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]} is defined twice'))\n   217\t        figs[fig['id']] = fig\n   218\t\n   219\t    def refs(fig):\n   220\t        out = list(fig.get('inputs', []))\n   221\t        out += [r for r in fig.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs or r not in passages]\n   222\t        if fig.get('adjusts'):\n   223\t            out.append(fig['adjusts']['figure'])\n   224\t        if fig.get('bridge'):\n   225\t            out.append(fig['bridge'])\n   226\t        return out\n   359\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{view_id} has {seen.get(view_id, 0)} answers; exactly one is required'))\n   360\t    for view_id in seen:\n   361\t        if view_id not in members:\n   362\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{view_id} is not a member of the family'))\n   363\t    outcomes = {}\n   364\t    for ans in calc['answers']:\n   365\t        member = members.get(ans['view_id'])\n   366\t        if member is None:\n   367\t            continue\n   368\t        if ans.get('shape') == 'unresolved':\n   369\t            if 'outcome' in ans or 'rung' in ans or not ans.get('why'):\n   370\t                errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: an unresolved answer has a reason and neither outcome nor rung'))\n   371\t            continue\n   372\t        out = figs.get(ans.get('outcome'))\n   373\t        if out is None:\n   374\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: outcome {ans.get(\"outcome\")} is not a figure'))\n   375\t            continue\n   376\t        if _key(out['what']) != _key(member['what']):\n   377\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: outcome {out[\"id\"]} measures {_key(out[\"what\"])}, not the question\\'s {_key(member[\"what\"])}'))\n   378\t        outcomes[ans['view_id']] = out['id']\n   379\t        rung = ans.get('rung')\n   380\t        if not isinstance(rung, int) or isinstance(rung, bool) or not 1 <= rung <= len(member['bands']):   # [46q] before any lookup\n   381\t            errors.append(('C6', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: rung {rung!r} is not one of 1..{len(member[\"bands\"])}'))\n   382\t            continue\n   383\t        band = member['bands'][rung - 1]\n   384\t        if not _overlaps(_outcome_set(out), band):                 # [46r] open and closed ends kept\n   385\t            errors.append(('C6', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: rung {rung} ({band}) contains no part of its outcome {_outcome_set(out)}'))\n   386\t        ref = ans.get('reference') or {}\n   387\t        if ('figure' in ref) == ('unavailable' in ref):          # [46g.2] exactly one choice\n   388\t            errors.append(('C5', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: the reference must name exactly one of a figure or unavailable'))\n   389\t        elif 'unavailable' in ref:\n   390\t            if not ref['unavailable']:\n   391\t                errors.append(('C5', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: an unavailable reference needs a reason'))\n   392\t        else:\n   393\t            errors += _reference_errors(ans['view_id'], figs.get(ref.get('figure')), figs, passages, refs)\n   394\t\n   395\t    # [46j.1] scenario membership derived from the estimates a figure rests on; related members cover the same scenarios\n   396\t    def scen(fid):\n   397\t        return figs[fid].get('scenario', 'base')\n   398\t\n   399\t    def derived(fid):\n   400\t        return {scen(g) for g in _upstream_of(fid, figs, refs) | {fid} if figs[g]['kind'] == 'estimate' and scen(g) != 'range'}\n   401\t    for f in figs.values():\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
