{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'approx_above|approx_below|nearly|more than' calc_check.py DESIGN.md REQUEST-AUDIT.md render_v13.py | head -40; sed -n '10,45p' calc_check.py; sed -n '423,451p' calc_check.py\"","aggregated_output":"render_v13.py:41:        'bound': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['>', '>=', '<', '<=', 'approx', 'approx_below', 'approx_above']}),\nrender_v13.py:45:                                'it, qualifiers included (for example \"more than $2 billion\", \"$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%\", \"more than triple\").'}),\nDESIGN.md:35:             value | {low, high} | {bound: \">\" | \">=\" | \"<\" | \"<=\" | \"approx\" | \"approx_below\" | \"approx_above\", value} | {multiplier, bound?},  unit,   # [46c.3]\nDESIGN.md:71:| **C1 source expression** [46b.2] | code extracts every complete numeric expression from the cited passage as shown, with its qualifiers and unit. Points: \"$108.0 billion\". Ranges: \"$105–110 billion\". Relative: \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\" is midpoint 108 ±2%. Bounds: \"more than $730 billion\" (>730), \"at least\" (>=). Approximate bounds: \"nearly $800 billion\" (approx_below 800). Multipliers: \"double\" ×2, \"more than double\" (>×2). A source figure names one extracted expression and a component of it (midpoint, low, high, bound, multiplier), and must equal it exactly: value, unit, sign and qualifier. Any other wording cannot be a source figure | a figure that strips a qualifier ($730 from \"more than $730 billion\"); a bound used as a point; a wrong number within 0.5% (108.5); a figure naming no extracted expression |\nDESIGN.md:85:| **C2 bound direction** [46f.3] | for positive operands, a result's bound side follows its inputs: sums and products keep a lower or upper side, a ratio's or difference's second operand flips it, and mixed sides give `approx` | \"more than double\" times $20B declared below $40B |\nDESIGN.md:160:| R3 | old-2 8595: 730 (e1786, bound \">\") / 800 (e2535, bound \"approx_below\") × 1,300 (e2535, point) | stripped qualifiers: **C1**. Qualifiers kept: passes C1, then **C8** without a bridge naming those operands. With the bridge: recorded, undetermined |\nDESIGN.md:161:| R4 | old-3 9166: 20 × (>2) (e3660, \"more than double\") gives >40, trimmed to 38–39 by `adjusts: trim` | recorded adjustment that definitely crosses the $40B boundary (rung 2 is $40–50B, rung 1 $50B+) |\nDESIGN.md:164:| T1–T7 (C1 forms, real passages) | e2499 midpoint 108 ±2% (accepted as `midpoint`); e1786 \">730\"; e2535 approx_below 800 and the point 1,300; e3660 \">×2\"; stripped forms \"$730\", \"800\", \"double\" against those passages; 108.5 against e2499 | T1–T3 parse as stated; the stripped forms and 108.5 refused |\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md:44:  example 'more than $2 billion', '$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%', 'more than triple')\". The examples come from no gate case [46f.4].\ncalc_check.py:12:QUAL = {'more than': '>', 'over': '>', 'at least': '>=', 'nearly': 'approx_below', 'almost': 'approx_below',\ncalc_check.py:26:    ('multiplier', re.compile(r'\\b(more than\\s+)?(double|triple)\\b', re.I)),\ncalc_check.py:145:DIRECTION = {'>': 'lower', '>=': 'lower', 'approx_above': 'lower', '<': 'upper', '<=': 'upper', 'approx_below': 'upper',\ncalc_check.py:170:    if b in ('>=', 'approx_above'):\ncalc_check.py:174:    if b in ('<=', 'approx_below'):\nimport re\n\nQUAL = {'more than': '>', 'over': '>', 'at least': '>=', 'nearly': 'approx_below', 'almost': 'approx_below',\n        'approximately': 'approx', 'about': 'approx', 'around': 'approx', 'roughly': 'approx',\n        'up to': '<=', 'less than': '<', 'below': '<', 'under': '<'}\nSCALE = {'trillion': 1000.0, 'tn': 1000.0, 't': 1000.0, 'billion': 1.0, 'bn': 1.0, 'b': 1.0, 'million': 0.001, 'm': 0.001}\nNUM = r'(\\d[\\d,]*(?:\\.\\d+)?)'\nUNIT = r'(trillion|billion|million|bn|tn|T|B|M)\\b'\nQWORDS = '|'.join(sorted(QUAL, key=len, reverse=True))\nPATTERNS = [\n    ('relative', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT + r',?\\s*(?:plus or minus|±)\\s*' + NUM + r'%')),\n    ('range', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*(?:' + UNIT + r')?\\s*(?:–|-)\\s*\\$?\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT)),   # \"to\" is ambiguous (\"from $253 billion to $392 billion\")\n    ('range', re.compile(r'\\bbetween\\s+\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*(?:' + UNIT + r')?\\s+and\\s+\\$?\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT, re.I)),\n    ('qualified', re.compile(r'\\b(' + QWORDS + r')\\s+\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT, re.I)),\n    ('money', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'\\s*' + UNIT)),\n    ('money_plain', re.compile(r'\\$\\s?' + NUM + r'(?![\\d,.]*\\s*(?:trillion|billion|million|bn|tn|T|B|M)\\b)')),\n    ('multiplier', re.compile(r'\\b(more than\\s+)?(double|triple)\\b', re.I)),\n    ('percent', re.compile(r'\\b(?:(' + QWORDS + r')\\s+)?' + NUM + r'%', re.I)),\n]\nOPERATIONS = {'sum', 'difference', 'product', 'ratio', 'growth', 'apply_growth', 'share', 'range_from_relative', 'roll_forward'}\nARITY = {'difference': (2, 2), 'ratio': (2, 2), 'growth': (2, 2), 'apply_growth': (2, 2), 'share': (2, 2), 'range_from_relative': (2, 2),\n         'product': (2, 99), 'sum': (1, 99), 'roll_forward': (2, 99)}          # [46m.1] every operand an operation lists is one it uses\nKINDS = {'source', 'computed', 'estimate', 'prior'}\nBASES = {'reported', 'guidance', 'consensus', 'third_party', 'forecast', 'prior_forecast'}\nEXTERNAL = {'consensus', 'guidance', 'third_party'}\n\n\ndef _num(text):\n    return float(text.replace(',', ''))\n\n\ndef _scale(unit):\n    return SCALE[unit.lower()] if unit else 1.0\n\n\ndef extract(text):\n\n    # C3 part within whole, C4 one forecast per shared quantity (every path)\n    def reachable(start, stop=None):\n        stops = set(stop) if isinstance(stop, (set, list, tuple)) else {stop}\n        seen_ids, stack = set(), [start]\n        while stack:\n            fid = stack.pop()\n            if fid in seen_ids or fid not in figs:\n                continue\n            seen_ids.add(fid)\n            if fid not in stops:\n                stack.extend(refs(figs[fid]))\n        return seen_ids\n    scenarios = {f.get('scenario', 'base') for f in figs.values() if f['basis'] == 'forecast'} or {'base'}\n    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n        if rel['type'] != 'part_of' or rel['part'] not in outcomes or rel['whole'] not in outcomes:\n            continue\n        part_m, whole_m = members[rel['part']], members[rel['whole']]\n        for sc in scenarios:\n            for period in family.get('compare_periods', []):\n                def node(view_id, member):\n                    want = (member['what']['population'], member['what']['measure'], member['what']['scope'], period)\n                    hits = [figs[f] for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id]) if _key(figs[f]['what']) == want\n                            and figs[f]['basis'] == 'forecast' and figs[f].get('scenario', 'base') == sc]\n                    return hits[0] if hits else None\n                p, w = node(rel['part'], part_m), node(rel['whole'], whole_m)\n                if p and w:\n                    (plo, phi), (wlo, whi) = _interval(p), _interval(w)\n                    if plo > wlo + 1e-9 or phi > whi + 1e-9:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport pathlib,json,io,contextlib,copy,types\nimport gate as g, calc_check as c, render_v13 as r, mutants\ndef replay(func, log):\n    p=io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(p): status=func()\n    assert status==0 and p.getvalue()==pathlib.Path(log).read_text()\nreplay(g.main,'\\\\''gate-run15.txt'\\\\'')\nassert g.MANIFEST==json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''gate-run15.fixtures.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nreplay(r.main,'\\\\''render-r1.txt'\\\\'')\noriginal=g.cc\npath=pathlib.Path('\\\\''calc_check.py'\\\\'')\nsrc=path.read_text()\nfor name,old,new,target in mutants.MUTANTS:\n    g.cc=original\n    if old:\n        assert src.count(old)==1,name\n        mod=types.ModuleType('\\\\''in_memory_calc_check'\\\\'')\n        exec(compile(src.replace(old,new),str(path),'\\\\''exec'\\\\''),mod.__dict__)\n        g.cc=mod\n    misses={name for name,ok,_,_ in g.run() if not ok}\n    assert (target in misses if target else not misses),(name,misses)\ng.cc=original\nprint('\\\\''65 gate items, 30 mutants and stored render reproduced'\\\\'')\ndef fig(x,fid):\n    return next(f for f in x['\\\\''figures'\\\\''] if f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']==fid)\ndef check(name,case,passages):\n    fam,x=case['\\\\''family'\\\\''],case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\n    schema=r.v13_schema(list(fam['\\\\''members'\\\\'']),list(passages),[])\n    wire=r.strict(x,schema)\n    clean=r.without_nulls(wire)\n    report=c.check(fam,passages,clean)\n    print(name, r.model.check_schema(wire,schema),report,c.publish_decision(fam,clean,report))\nfor name in ('\\\\''R4'\\\\'','\\\\''R4b2'\\\\'','\\\\''R4b3'\\\\''):\n    check(name,g.MANIFEST[name],g.R4_PASSAGES)\ncase=copy.deepcopy(g.MANIFEST['\\\\''R1c'\\\\''])\nx=case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\ndcq4=fig(x,'\\\\''dcq4'\\\\'')\nx['\\\\''figures'\\\\''].remove(dcq4)\nx['\\\\''figures'\\\\''].append(g.est('\\\\''dcq4'\\\\'',127.1,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',dcq4['\\\\''what'\\\\''],'\\\\''Data Center exceeds \"'$127.1B even after discounting'\"'\\\\'', ['\\\\''e976'\\\\''],bound='\\\\''>'\\\\''))\nfig(x,'\\\\''dcfy'\\\\'').update(value=396.1,bound='\\\\''>'\\\\'')\ncheck('\\\\''R1 inequality with equal thresholds, strict part greater than point whole'\\\\'',case,g.R1_PASSAGES)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
